  "prompt": "I have 5 completely independent work streams to run in parallel. NOTHING is given to you directly — every value and identifier lives in the system's records and must be resolved by following references from one record to the next. For each item, start from the named worklist and dereference step by step until you reach the concrete value, then act. (A) TRACK COVERAGE: From coverage worklist `watch_candidates_wl2`, add each coverage candidate that is NOT delisted (skip any with delisted on its dereferenced record — the list mixes delisted and near-duplicate when-issued look-alikes). For each real one, resolve every value it requires by following the record references, then add it to the watchlist. Then, from worklist `set_linked_bank_account_wl1`, set the settlement linked bank account: pick the real item (SKIP the superseded look-alike), then resolve every value it requires by following the record references, and act with those resolved values (never the worklist ref itself). (B) PRUNE WATCHLIST: From prune worklist `prune_list_wl2`, remove each watchlist entry that is NOT reinstated (skip reinstated on its dereferenced record — near-duplicate look-alikes are listed too). For each, resolve every value it requires by following the record references, then remove it. Then, from worklist `place_market_order_wl1`, place the coverage market order: pick the real item (SKIP the superseded look-alike), then resolve every value it requires by following the record references, and act with those resolved values (never the worklist ref itself). (C) CANCEL STALE ORDERS: From stale-order worklist `stale_orders_wl2`, cancel each stale order that is NOT already closed (skip already_closed on its dereferenced record). For each, resolve every value it requires by following the record references, then cancel it. Then, from worklist `place_stop_order_wl1`, place the protective stop order: pick the real item (SKIP the superseded look-alike), then resolve every value it requires by following the record references, and act with those resolved values (never the worklist ref itself). (D) SCHEDULE SWEEPS: From sweep worklist `sweep_instructions_wl2`, schedule each active recurring sweep that is NOT cancelled (skip cancelled on its dereferenced record). For each, resolve every value it requires by following the record references, then schedule the withdrawal. Then, from worklist `wire_withdrawal_wl1`, wire the expedited settlement cash: pick the real item (SKIP the superseded look-alike), then resolve every value it requires by following the record references, and act with those resolved values (never the worklist ref itself). (E) STAGE LIMIT ORDERS: From limit-ticket worklist `limit_tickets_wl2`, place each staged limit-sell ticket that is NOT already filled (skip already_filled on its dereferenced record). For each, resolve every value it requires by following the record references, then place the limit sell. Then, from worklist `modify_order_wl1`, modify the resting limit order: pick the real item (SKIP the superseded look-alike), then resolve every value it requires by following the record references, and act with those resolved values (never the worklist ref itself). None of these 5 streams depend on each other, so run them concurrently. For EVERY item: resolve each target FRESH by chaining through the records at the moment you act — never guess, and never reuse a value you read earlier.",
